    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the route-deviation claim is upheld and the full contested fare of SGD 27.50 is refunded to the rider.\n\nROUTE. The governing actual distance is the GPS trace figure, 18.96 km (EV-GPS-04009); POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern and forbids citing the rounded 19.0 km convenience copy on the trip record for the threshold test. The booked optimal route is 10.3 km (EV-TRIP-04009), so the excess is 8.66 km — 84.1% of the optimal route. That clears both establishment tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km) and both materiality tests (over 50% and over 8.0 km).\n\nTRACE INTEGRITY. The trace is impaired at schema level: it carries issue GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW at weight_multiplier 0.85 (a 70-second gap from 23:16:50 to 23:18:00 just after the trip started, bounding fixes 194.6 m apart). The impairment is disclosed, and the finding survives it: the trace meets none of the policy-level limbs in POL-RD-07 (gap over 90 s, jump over 500 m, sustained interval over 30 s), so it is down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 only and remains fit to establish the deviation without independent corroboration.\n\nDRIVER'S EXPLANATION. The driver's account that he used the expressway at night because it is faster is an external-cause assertion with no record behind it. The only traffic-advisory identifier in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-04009-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and, under POL-RD-13, the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08; no advisory was on file and that explanation is discarded. No rider-requested detour arises either — there is no chat log for the trip (EV-CHAT-04009, MISSING at weight 0.0), so POL-RD-04 cannot be run — and no POL-RD-05 amendment or POL-RD-12 pooled itinerary applies.\n\nMONEY. The fare model is METERED with surge_multiplier 1.0, read from the fare_breakdown, so POL-RD-02 applies. On the booked optimal route the recomputed fare is (3.80 + 0.75 × 10.3 + 0.28 × 17) × 1.0 + 0.80 = SGD 17.085, against a charged_total of SGD 27.50 — a POL-RD-02 partial refund of SGD 10.415, rounded up to SGD 10.45 (37.9% of the amount charged).\n\nUPLIFT. The driver profile records deviation_flags_90d of 4 against completed_trips_90d of 380, so the repeat-deviation pattern in POL-RD-06 is established on the citable trailing-window fields. Because this deviation is material and substantiated on this trip's own evidence, POL-RD-06(b) lifts the remedy from the POL-RD-02 partial of SGD 10.45 to a FULL_REFUND of the charged_total, SGD 27.50; the two figures are stated side by side so the size of the uplift is auditable. There are no ERP or surcharge pass-through lines to carve out (all zero), so the whole contested amount is refunded.\n\nREFERRAL. The same pattern requires the case to go to driver-conduct review under POL-RD-06(c). That is a referral riding with the money ruling, not an escalation, and it does not delay the payment.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. The deciding fact — the excess distance — rests on the single trace at weight 0.85, so confidence is capped at 0.85 under POL-GEN-02(2), above the 0.70 escalation floor. The refund of SGD 27.50 exceeds the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so it is issued but held for release by a human reviewer under POL-GEN-05."
