    "explanation": "To both parties. This was a metered RYDE_TAXI trip on 19 Sep 2026 from Gardens by the Bay to Holland Village. The platform booked an optimal route of 10.3 km / 17 min (EV-TRIP-04009); the driver's GPS trace records 18.96 km / 31 min (EV-GPS-04009). Under POL-RD-01 the governing distance is gps_trace.trace_distance_km, 18.96 km, not the rounded 19.0 km convenience copy on the trip record. Excess = 18.96 − 10.3 = 8.66 km, i.e. 84.08% of the optimal route. Both establishment tests pass (84.08% > 20%; 8.66 km > 0.8 km) and both materiality limbs fire (84.08% > 50%; 8.66 km > 8.0 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. Trace integrity: EV-GPS-04009 is impaired at the admissibility layer — weight_multiplier 0.85, issue GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW (a 70 s gap from 23:16:50 to 23:18:00, bounding fixes 194.6 m apart, at the start of the trip). POL-RD-07 sets its own, looser thresholds (gap over 90 s, jump over 500 m, sustained interval over 30 s), and this trace fails all three. It is therefore schema-impaired but NOT impaired for policy purposes: no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The finding survives the POL-GEN-02 discount. Driver's explanation: the statement 'night time I use expressway because faster' asserts an external traffic cause but names no traffic advisory. EV-ADVIS-04009-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0); under POL-RD-13 the three-part comparison POL-RD-03 requires cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver cites no advisory identifier, the missing artifact is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. No rider-requested detour can be made out either: EV-CHAT-04009 is MISSING (weight 0.0), POL-RD-04 cannot run, and the driver's own statement concedes no instruction was given. No POL-RD-05 relocation applies (pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null) and no POL-RD-12 pooled itinerary applies (vehicle_type is RYDE_TAXI), so the booked 10.3 km optimal stands as the comparator. Money: the fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not run. Reading surge_multiplier from EV-FARE-04009 as 1.0, the POL-RD-02 recomputation on the booked optimal is (3.80 + 0.75 × 10.3 + 0.28 × 17) × 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 17.085, against a charged_total of 27.50 — a baseline POL-RD-02 refund of 10.415, rounded up to 10.45. That baseline is not the outcome. The deviation is MATERIAL and is substantiated on this trip's own evidence, and the POL-RD-06 pattern test is met on the citable fields (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 4, which is 3 or more; the ratio test is not needed because the clause is disjunctive, and I do not use the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter). POL-RD-06(b) therefore applies and lifts the remedy to FULL_REFUND of charged_total 27.50 in place of the 10.45 partial. The uplift is confined to distance and time lines, and the pass-through side is already empty — ERP 0.00, airport surcharge 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0.00, promo_discount 0.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 — so the full 27.50 moves and nothing is double-counted under POL-RD-09. Confidence: the deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-04009 (0.85, the excess distance) and EV-TRIP-04009 (1.0, the optimal distance). The excess is not independently carried — the fare ledger's 18.96 km and the trip record's 19.0 km are both copies of the same trace measurement, so they are one carrier, not two — and the cap is accordingly the minimum, 0.85, which is above the 0.70 floor. Execution: the monetary effect of 27.50 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of 8.00, so the ruling issues but the amount is held for release by the human queue.",
